After reviewing the current `ethonline-2026` branch, the Letta MVP plan, the real TypeScript Letta runtime, the Lab/Hydra code, worker lineage, `.af` snapshots, `cg`, and the older `mwgo` branch, most of the primitives already exist. The problem is that they are split across two generations of implementation. The ETHOnline branch now has the real stack: Letta Agent SDK runtime, Lab pipeline, reflection, trajectory, worker lineage, `.af` packaging, DSSE/Merkle evidence, encryption/keybroker, and 138 tests.

The next job is **consolidation into one runnable product**.

## The architecture I would freeze

Your core idea is right, with two terminology/implementation corrections:

```text
                           MOLTWORK LAB
                               │
                 ┌─────────────┴──────────────┐
                 │                            │
              ORACLE                     INVENTORY
        opportunities anywhere        accumulated capital
                 │                            ▲
                 ▼                            │
             WorkOrder                       │
                 │                            │
                 ▼                            │
          Portfolio decision                  │
                 │                            │
                 ▼                            │
         Git worktree / branch                │
                 │                            │
                 ▼                            │
       persistent Letta Worker                │
       same Agent, new Conversation           │
                 │                            │
        ┌────────┼────────┐                   │
        ▼        ▼        ▼                   │
      tools    skills   Lab Brief             │
        │        │        │                   │
        └────────┼────────┘                   │
                 ▼                            │
            WorkerKit                         │
     events / costs / evidence                │
                 │                            │
                 ▼                            │
           Verification                       │
                 │                            │
                 ▼                            │
            CommitGate                        │
                 │                            │
       ┌─────────┴─────────┐                  │
       ▼                   ▼                  │
   submission          run closed             │
       │                   │                  │
       ▼                   ├── trajectory ────┤
 outcome/payment           ├── review ────────┤
       │                   ├── modules ───────┤
       └───────────────────┴── learning ──────┘
                                    │
                                    ▼
                              Letta reflection
                                    │
                              LearningProposal
                                    │
                                    ▼
                                    cg
                            held-out A/B evaluation
                                    │
                              PASS / REJECT
                                    │
                                    ▼
                            new MemFS Git commit
                                    │
                                    ▼
                           WorkerManifest vN+1
```

The two corrections are important.

**First, `.af` is not the economic receipt format.** `.af` is the portable snapshot/package of the Letta worker. Your economic/evidence receipts should remain JCS/DSSE/Merkle content-addressed statements. The current ETHOnline branch already has separate DSSE/Merkle and `.af` machinery, which is the right separation.

So:

```text
RECEIPTS/*.dsse.json
    = what happened economically / evidentially

SNAPSHOTS/*.af
    = what this worker version is

WorkerManifest
    = exact bill of materials tying them together
```

**Second, don't literally treat Letta MemFS as an ordinary folder inside the parent Git repository.** MemFS is itself Git-backed and Letta owns its history. Letta documents MemFS as long-term Git-backed memory, while the current Agent SDK gives you persistent Agents with new Conversations/Sessions for individual jobs. ([GitHub][1])

The parent Lab Git repository should record the **MemFS commit SHA**, not attempt to absorb its `.git` directory.

That gives you four clearly separated truth domains:

| Domain                      | Source of truth                 |
| --------------------------- | ------------------------------- |
| Work produced               | Git commit/tree                 |
| Worker learning             | Letta MemFS Git commit          |
| Execution facts             | WorkerKit EventLedger           |
| Economic/evidence statement | DSSE/Merkle WorkerKit receipt   |
| Search/analytics            | HydraDB, rebuildable            |
| Portable worker             | `.af` snapshot + WorkerManifest |

That is the architecture.

