# 7. Fix the runtime service before building anything else

The current TS service is the right skeleton, but it needs four important changes.

### A. Stream execution instead of returning everything at the end

Right now it collects output/tool calls and returns the result after the Session ends.

You want:

```text
Letta SDK stream
      │
      ▼
runtime-letta
      │
      ├─ assistant.delta
      ├─ tool.call
      ├─ tool.result
      ├─ model.usage
      ├─ artifact
      └─ error
      │
      ▼
WorkerKit EventLedger
```

Prefer NDJSON or WebSocket.

Then a run isn't:

```text
Agent says what it did
→ WorkerKit records summary
```

It is:

```text
Agent does something
→ WorkerKit witnesses event
```

Much stronger.

### B. Do not use `permissionMode: "approve-all"`

The current runtime does.

Instead translate the WorkOrder policy into Letta's session-scoped `toolset` and `allowedTools`. Letta explicitly documents `allowedTools` as the final visibility boundary, and the SDK also exposes interactive `canUseTool` authorization. ([GitHub][1])

The hierarchy should be:

```text
WorkOrder Policy
       │
       ▼
allowedTools
       │
       ▼
tool call
       │
       ▼
canUseTool
       │
  risky action?
    /       \
   no       yes
   │         │
 allow      WorkerKit authorization
             │
           Warrant
             │
         CommitGate
```

So Moltwork doesn't merely *ask* the agent not to submit or spend.

It technically can't.

### C. Never allow ordinary work runs to rewrite durable memory

Disable dreaming/automatic promotion in ordinary paid runs initially.

The production worker receives its current MemFS state read-only in spirit.

Learning happens later through:

```text
Reflection → proposal → experiment → promotion
```

Your current MVP plan already says exactly this.

### D. Remove prompt-based learning application

The current `/learning` endpoint tells the worker:

> update this memory

or:

> create this SKILL.md

via an agent message.

Don't use that as the production promotion mechanism.

A validated learning patch should be applied **deterministically to Git**.

More on that below.

