# 16. Hydra is the Lab brain, but not its memory

This distinction is subtle but essential.

Real HydraDB is very useful here because Moltwork naturally produces a graph:

```text
Worker
  │
  ├── HAS_VERSION ── WorkerVersion
  │                      │
  │                      ├── USED_SKILL ── SkillVersion
  │                      ├── MEMORY ─────── MemoryRevision
  │                      └── PARENT ─────── WorkerVersion
  │
  └── EXECUTED ── Run
                    │
                    ├── TARGETED ── Opportunity
                    ├── USED ────── ProcessVersion
                    ├── USED ────── Model
                    ├── RECEIVED ── LabBrief
                    ├── PRODUCED ── Artifact
                    ├── VERIFIED ── Verification
                    ├── RECEIPT ─── Receipt
                    └── OUTCOME ─── Outcome
```

Learning adds:

```text
Run ── SUPPORTS ── LearningProposal
                       │
                       ▼
                   Experiment
                       │
                    VALIDATES
                       │
                       ▼
                  WorkerVersion
```

Assets add:

```text
Artifact
    │
 DERIVED_INTO
    ▼
AssetVersion
    │
