vs
Worker v2

same unseen tasks

quality ↑
cost ↓ / bounded
time ↓
no gate regression
```

The Letta MVP document already defines essentially this experiment.

If that passes, Moltwork has demonstrated something substantially stronger than “we connected an agent to gigs.”

It has demonstrated:

> **A persistent economic worker can encounter unfamiliar forms of work, accumulate verified experience in Git, turn repeated experience into validated procedural capital, and use that capital to become economically better at future work.**

And the `mwgo` proposition becomes extremely clean:

```bash
npx mwgo init my-lab
```

means, in one command:

```text
give me
a durable worker
+ a Git workshop
+ persistent Letta cognition
+ WorkerKit economic truth
+ a learning Lab
+ a rebuildable Hydra graph
+ verified lineage
+ an inventory that compounds
```

That is the version I would build. The architecture is now mature enough that I would stop designing alternative stacks and make `mwgo init → first real unseen WorkOrder → learned Worker v2` the primary engineering path.

